# https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/startTime node403
node403 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>startTime</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/startTime' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/startTime</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;The point in time when an element or an action starts,
becomes applicable, or becomes valid.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;The point in time when an element or an action starts,
becomes applicable, or becomes valid.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;A timestamp marking the commencement of an action,
the beginning of an element&#x27;s relevance,
or the intended start of either.

It encompasses the moment of triggering processes,
such as build executions or service instantiations,
as well as the point in time when an element
or a relationship between elements becomes effective or active.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
